# Ownership of every path in this repository.
#
# A single maintainer today, so the value of this file is not routing — it is that GitHub requests a
# review on every pull request, including ones opened by automation. The explicit blocks below are
# the paths where an unreviewed change is most expensive, kept separate so that intent survives if
# this ever becomes a team.

*                       @dgfigueroa29

# The contract for agents and the harness that enforces it. A change here changes how every future
# change gets made.
/AGENTS.md              @dgfigueroa29
/CLAUDE.md              @dgfigueroa29
/.claude/               @dgfigueroa29

# Decisions already taken. These are never rewritten — a superseding ADR is the only way to change
# one, and that is a decision in itself.
/docs/adr/              @dgfigueroa29

# Source of truth. `docs/ENGINES.md` is compared against `ScannerEngineCatalog` by a test.
/docs/                  @dgfigueroa29
/openspec/              @dgfigueroa29

# The privacy guarantee lives here: no INTERNET permission, allowBackup false, dataExtractionRules
# present. `tools/checks.py` enforces it, and this line makes sure a human sees it too.
/androidApp/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml   @dgfigueroa29
/docs/legal/            @dgfigueroa29

# What is verified, and how. A weakened check is worse than a missing one, because it reads as
# coverage.
/.github/workflows/     @dgfigueroa29
/tools/                 @dgfigueroa29
/config/detekt/         @dgfigueroa29

# The SPI. Every engine depends on it, and a change here is a change to nine modules.
/core/scanner-api/      @dgfigueroa29
/core/scanner-testing/  @dgfigueroa29
